  "description": "Meta-package bundling TINS.Native.FFTW.win-x64, TINS.Native.FFTW.linux-x64, and TINS.Native.FFTW.osx-arm64, so a multi-platform consumer that has already decided to accept FFTW's GPL-2.0-or-later obligation can pull in FFTW for every built desktop RID with a single reference instead of adding each RID package individually. A single-RID deployment should still reference just its own TINS.Native.FFTW.<rid> package directly -- this carries no native content of its own. osx-x64 is deliberately excluded (see the PackageReference comment below), unlike the core TINS.Native.Desktop package, which does include a placeholder for it.",
